window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b237-951e98758cb15774.json"]={sha256:"951e98758cb15774c6d2c59afad36d4134b9ca2f30549fe25cdbf260a2841c0e",value:{"id":"b237","title":"壩基帷幕灌漿","titleEn":"Dam-foundation curtain grouting","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以壩基帷幕灌漿為入口，深入裂隙可灌性、有效注入壓力與帷幕驗證。十個單元各自對應不同的荷載路徑、能量交換或監測問題，從守恆式建立量化估算，再檢查量測配置是否能辨認真正失效原因。工程史實只採用列明範圍的公開一手資料；所有模型輸入另標為教學假設，成果是可追溯的工程判讀紀錄。","summaryEn":"Using Dam-foundation curtain grouting as its entry point, this course examines fracture groutability, effective injection pressure and curtain verification. Ten units address different load paths, energy exchanges or monitoring questions, starting with conservation-based estimates and testing whether observations distinguish failure causes. Historical statements use scoped primary evidence. Numerical model inputs are separately identified as teaching assumptions, producing a traceable engineering interpretation record.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-systems","subcategoryTitle":"防潮、航運與大壩施工","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tidal barriers, navigation and dam construction","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-systems","learningTags":["water","water-systems","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["裂隙開度與流量","Fracture aperture and flow"],["降伏應力與滲入距離","Yield stress and penetration length"],["岩體抬動與壓力邊界","Rock jacking and pressure boundaries"],["壓水試驗標準化","Water-test normalization"],["獨立驗證與統計分布","Independent verification and distributions"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-dam","labels":["裂隙開度與流量","降伏應力與滲入距離","岩體抬動與壓力邊界","壓水試驗標準化","獨立驗證與統計分布"],"labelsEn":["Fracture aperture and flow","Yield stress and penetration length","Rock jacking and pressure boundaries","Water-test normalization","Independent verification and distributions"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課原創比較練習分兩個相互獨立的物理模型。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設相同壓差下開度由0.1增至0.15 mm，理想流量比(0.15/0.1)³=3.375；牛頓流體層流，不直接代表含顆粒漿液。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設裂隙開度0.2 mm、顆粒d95=0.04 mm，開度粒徑比5；不將此數字當通用可灌門檻，也不推定現地可達距離。先逐一圈出公式內的控制體、力方向或時間尺度，再把每項輸入的量綱換成一致單位。第二人只根據輸入重算結果，不抄第一人的中間數字。最後指出這兩個估算尚未包含的空間變化、非線性及量測誤差；若將結果用於另一座工程，必須重建其幾何、材料與邊界條件，不能挪用本練習的假設。","textEn":"This original comparison exercise uses two independent physical models. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume aperture rises from 0.1 to 0.15 mm at equal pressure gradient. Ideal flow ratio is 3.375 for laminar Newtonian flow, not directly for particle-bearing grout. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fracture aperture 0.2 mm and particle d95=0.04 mm, giving aperture-to-particle ratio five. This is not a universal groutability limit or a prediction of field reach. First identify the control volume, force direction or time scale in each relation, then convert every input to consistent units. A second reviewer recalculates from the inputs without copying intermediate numbers. Finally identify spatial variability, nonlinear effects and measurement errors omitted by both estimates. Transfer to another structure requires rebuilding its geometry, material description and boundary conditions; the assumed classroom inputs are not transferable design or operating parameters.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b237-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「裂隙開度與流量」與「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fracture aperture and flow\" and \"Particle size and groutability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b237-v15-01","title":"裂隙開度與流量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「裂隙開度與流量」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fracture aperture and flow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"薄裂隙的層流流量對水力開度高度敏感，微小張開可造成大流量變化。平行板立方律只是理想模型，粗糙、接觸點與通道化會改變實際通水性。 假設相同壓差下開度由0.1增至0.15 mm，理想流量比(0.15/0.1)³=3.375；牛頓流體層流，不直接代表含顆粒漿液。 把水力開度當作幾何平均寬度會錯估可灌性，壓力上升也可能改變裂隙本身。若只用一次流量反算唯一開度，會掩蓋多通道等效結果的不唯一性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「裂隙開度與流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Laminar flow through a thin fracture is highly sensitive to hydraulic aperture. The parallel-plate cubic law is idealized; roughness, contacts and channeling change actual conductivity and can dominate the measured response. Assume aperture rises from 0.1 to 0.15 mm at equal pressure gradient. Ideal flow ratio is 3.375 for laminar Newtonian flow, not directly for particle-bearing grout. Hydraulic aperture is not geometric mean width, and pressure can change the fracture itself. Inferring one unique aperture from one flow measurement hides the nonuniqueness of several equivalent conducting channels. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fracture aperture and flow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設相同壓差下開度由0.1增至0.15 mm，理想流量比(0.15/0.1)³=3.375；牛頓流體層流，不直接代表含顆粒漿液。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume aperture rises from 0.1 to 0.15 mm at equal pressure gradient.","failure":"常見誤解：「水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「裂隙開度與流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fracture aperture and flow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-01-k1","title":"裂隙開度與流量","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow","text":"薄裂隙的層流流量對水力開度高度敏感，微小張開可造成大流量變化。平行板立方律只是理想模型，粗糙、接觸點與通道化會改變實際通水性。","textEn":"Laminar flow through a thin fracture is highly sensitive to hydraulic aperture. The parallel-plate cubic law is idealized; roughness, contacts and channeling change actual conductivity and can dominate the measured response.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「裂隙開度與流量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fracture aperture and flow\" is correct?","options":["水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。","薄裂隙的層流流量對水力開度高度敏感，微小張開可造成大流量變化。","只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。"],"optionsEn":["Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture.","Laminar flow through a thin fracture is highly sensitive to hydraulic aperture.","Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄裂隙的層流流量對水力開度高度敏感，微小張開可造成大流量變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Laminar flow through a thin fracture is highly sensitive to hydraulic aperture. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b237-v15-02","title":"裂隙開度與流量：定量估算","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「裂隙開度與流量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fracture aperture and flow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設相同壓差下開度由0.1增至0.15 mm，理想流量比(0.15/0.1)³=3.375；牛頓流體層流，不直接代表含顆粒漿液。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume aperture rises from 0.1 to 0.15 mm at equal pressure gradient. Ideal flow ratio is 3.375 for laminar Newtonian flow, not directly for particle-bearing grout. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以不同水頭測試流量線性並核對升降壓遲滯，將水試與漿試結果分開；對照孔壁裂隙和示蹤連通資料，確認流量變化不是封塞漏流或裂隙被壓開。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test flow linearity at several heads and compare loading-unloading hysteresis, separating water and grout tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設相同壓差下開度由0.1增至0.15 mm，理想流量比(0.15/0.1)³=3.375；牛頓流體層流，不直接代表含顆粒漿液。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume aperture rises from 0.1 to 0.15 mm at equal pressure gradient. Ideal flow ratio is 3.375 for laminar Newtonian flow, not directly for particle-bearing grout.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「裂隙開度與流量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fracture aperture and flow\", which statement holds?","options":["泵端表壓可不經高程和地下水修正直接當成孔段有效壓力。","供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設相同壓差下開度由0.1增至0.15 mm，理想流量比(0.15/0.1)³=3.375。"],"optionsEn":["Pump gauge pressure directly equals effective stage pressure without elevation or groundwater correction.","Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume aperture rises from 0.1 to 0.15 mm at equal pressure gradient."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設相同壓差下開度由0.1增至0.15 mm，理想流量比(0.15/0.1)³=3.375；牛頓流體層流，不直接代表含顆粒漿液。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume aperture rises from 0.1 to 0.15 mm at equal pressure gradient. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b237-v15-03","title":"裂隙開度與流量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「裂隙開度與流量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fracture aperture and flow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以不同水頭測試流量線性並核對升降壓遲滯，將水試與漿試結果分開；對照孔壁裂隙和示蹤連通資料，確認流量變化不是封塞漏流或裂隙被壓開。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test flow linearity at several heads and compare loading-unloading hysteresis, separating water and grout tests. Check mapped fractures and tracer connections and rule out packer leakage or pressure-induced opening before interpreting aperture changes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以裂隙開度與流量編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以不同水頭測試流量線性並核對升降壓遲滯，將水試與漿試結果分開；對照孔壁裂隙和示蹤連通資料，確認流量變化不是封塞漏流或裂隙被壓開。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for fracture aperture and flow, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Test flow linearity at several heads and compare loading-unloading hysteresis, separating water and grout tests. Check mapped fractures and tracer connections and rule out packer leakage or pressure-induced opening before interpreting aperture changes.","failure":"注意干擾：把水力開度當作幾何平均寬度會錯估可灌性，壓力上升也可能改變裂隙本身。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Hydraulic aperture is not geometric mean width, and pressure can change the fracture itself. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以不同水頭測試流量線性並核對升降壓遲滯，將水試與漿試結果分開；對照孔壁裂隙和示蹤連通資料，確認流量變化不是封塞漏流或裂隙被壓開。","textEn":"Test flow linearity at several heads and compare loading-unloading hysteresis, separating water and grout tests. Check mapped fractures and tracer connections and rule out packer leakage or pressure-induced opening before interpreting aperture changes.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以裂隙開度與流量編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以不同水頭測試流量線性並核對升降壓遲滯，將水試與漿試結果分開；對照孔壁裂隙和示蹤連通資料，確認流量變化不是封塞漏流或裂隙被壓開。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for fracture aperture and flow, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Test flow linearity at several heads and compare loading-unloading hysteresis, separating water and grout tests. Check mapped fractures and tracer connections and rule out packer leakage or pressure-induced opening before interpreting aperture changes.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「裂隙開度與流量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fracture aperture and flow\"?","options":["以不同水頭測試流量線性並核對升降壓遲滯，將水試與漿試結果分開；對照孔壁裂隙和示蹤連通資料，確認流量變化不是封塞漏流或裂隙被壓開。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。"],"optionsEn":["Test flow linearity at several heads and compare loading-unloading hysteresis, separating water and grout tests.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以不同水頭測試流量線性並核對升降壓遲滯，將水試與漿試結果分開；對照孔壁裂隙和示蹤連通資料，確認流量變化不是封塞漏流或裂隙被壓開。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test flow linearity at several heads and compare loading-unloading hysteresis, separating water and grout tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b237-v15-04","title":"裂隙開度與流量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「裂隙開度與流量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fracture aperture and flow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把水力開度當作幾何平均寬度會錯估可灌性，壓力上升也可能改變裂隙本身。若只用一次流量反算唯一開度，會掩蓋多通道等效結果的不唯一性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Hydraulic aperture is not geometric mean width, and pressure can change the fracture itself. Inferring one unique aperture from one flow measurement hides the nonuniqueness of several equivalent conducting channels. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只用一次流量反算唯一開度，會掩蓋多通道等效結果的不唯一性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Inferring one unique aperture from one flow measurement hides the nonuniqueness of several equivalent conducting channels.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把水力開度當作幾何平均寬度會錯估可灌性，壓力上升也可能改變裂隙本身。若只用一次流量反算唯一開度，會掩蓋多通道等效結果的不唯一性。","textEn":"Hydraulic aperture is not geometric mean width, and pressure can change the fracture itself. Inferring one unique aperture from one flow measurement hides the nonuniqueness of several equivalent conducting channels.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「裂隙開度與流量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fracture aperture and flow\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把水力開度當作幾何平均寬度會錯估可灌性，壓力上升也可能改變裂隙本身。","只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Hydraulic aperture is not geometric mean width, and pressure can change the fracture itself.","Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把水力開度當作幾何平均寬度會錯估可灌性，壓力上升也可能改變裂隙本身。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Hydraulic aperture is not geometric mean width, and pressure can change the fracture itself. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b237-v15-05","title":"顆粒尺寸與可灌性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Particle size and groutability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Particle size and groutability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水能通過的裂隙未必能讓水泥顆粒通過，顆粒架橋與濾餅會限制滲入。粒徑與開度比只能做篩選，還需考慮聚集、形狀和流變。 假設裂隙開度0.2 mm、顆粒d95=0.04 mm，開度粒徑比5；不將此數字當通用可灌門檻，也不推定現地可達距離。 細度證書不能代表混合後沒有團聚，孔口濾堵可能讓壓力上升卻沒有深部填充。若把高注入壓力當成帷幕密實證據，便可能掩蓋入口附近的局部封堵。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A water-conducting fracture may exclude cement grains. Bridging and filter-cake formation limit penetration, while particle-to-aperture ratio is only screening evidence because agglomeration, shape and rheology also matter. Assume fracture aperture 0.2 mm and particle d95=0.04 mm, giving aperture-to-particle ratio five. This is not a universal groutability limit or a prediction of field reach. A fineness certificate does not exclude agglomeration after mixing. Entrance filtration can raise pressure without deep filling, so high injection pressure alone can conceal a locally blocked entrance rather than a continuous curtain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Particle size and groutability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設裂隙開度0.2 mm、顆粒d95=0.04 mm，開度粒徑比5；不將此數字當通用可灌門檻，也不推定現地可達距離。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fracture aperture 0.2 mm and particle d95=0.04 mm, giving aperture-to-particle ratio five.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Particle size and groutability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-05-k1","title":"顆粒尺寸與可灌性","titleEn":"Particle size and groutability","text":"水能通過的裂隙未必能讓水泥顆粒通過，顆粒架橋與濾餅會限制滲入。粒徑與開度比只能做篩選，還需考慮聚集、形狀和流變。","textEn":"A water-conducting fracture may exclude cement grains. Bridging and filter-cake formation limit penetration, while particle-to-aperture ratio is only screening evidence because agglomeration, shape and rheology also matter.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Particle size and groutability\" is correct?","options":["只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。","漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。","水能通過的裂隙未必能讓水泥顆粒通過，顆粒架橋與濾餅會限制滲入。"],"optionsEn":["Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture.","Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient.","A water-conducting fracture may exclude cement grains."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水能通過的裂隙未必能讓水泥顆粒通過，顆粒架橋與濾餅會限制滲入。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A water-conducting fracture may exclude cement grains. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b237-v15-06","title":"顆粒尺寸與可灌性：定量估算","titleEn":"Particle size and groutability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Particle size and groutability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設裂隙開度0.2 mm、顆粒d95=0.04 mm，開度粒徑比5；不將此數字當通用可灌門檻，也不推定現地可達距離。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fracture aperture 0.2 mm and particle d95=0.04 mm, giving aperture-to-particle ratio five. This is not a universal groutability limit or a prediction of field reach. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對實際混合漿液的粒徑與聚集狀態，用代表性裂隙試驗比較進出漿濃度；觀察壓力升高是否伴隨流量降低和濾餅形成，再與水試的通水性分別判讀。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check particle size and agglomeration in the mixed grout and compare inlet and outlet concentration in representative fracture tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設裂隙開度0.2 mm、顆粒d95=0.04 mm，開度粒徑比5；不將此數字當通用可灌門檻，也不推定現地可達距離。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fracture aperture 0.2 mm and particle d95=0.04 mm, giving aperture-to-particle ratio five. This is not a universal groutability limit or a prediction of field reach.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Particle size and groutability\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設裂隙開度0.2 mm、顆粒d95=0.04 mm，開度粒徑比5；不將此數字當通用可灌門檻，也不推定現地可達距離。","吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。","標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fracture aperture 0.2 mm and particle d95=0.04 mm, giving aperture-to-particle ratio five.","A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling.","Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設裂隙開度0.2 mm、顆粒d95=0.04 mm，開度粒徑比5；不將此數字當通用可灌門檻，也不推定現地可達距離。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fracture aperture 0.2 mm and particle d95=0.04 mm, giving aperture-to-particle ratio five. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b237-v15-07","title":"顆粒尺寸與可灌性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Particle size and groutability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Particle size and groutability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對實際混合漿液的粒徑與聚集狀態，用代表性裂隙試驗比較進出漿濃度；觀察壓力升高是否伴隨流量降低和濾餅形成，再與水試的通水性分別判讀。檢查回漿是否富含細料。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check particle size and agglomeration in the mixed grout and compare inlet and outlet concentration in representative fracture tests. Observe pressure rise with declining flow and cake formation, keeping interpretation separate from water conductivity. Check whether returned grout is enriched in fines. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以顆粒尺寸與可灌性編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對實際混合漿液的粒徑與聚集狀態，用代表性裂隙試驗比較進出漿濃度；觀察壓力升高是否伴隨流量降低和濾餅形成，再與水試的通水性分別判讀。檢查回漿是否富含細料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for particle size and groutability, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check particle size and agglomeration in the mixed grout and compare inlet and outlet concentration in representative fracture tests. Observe pressure rise with declining flow and cake formation, keeping interpretation separate from water conductivity. Check whether returned grout is enriched in fines.","failure":"注意干擾：細度證書不能代表混合後沒有團聚，孔口濾堵可能讓壓力上升卻沒有深部填充。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A fineness certificate does not exclude agglomeration after mixing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對實際混合漿液的粒徑與聚集狀態，用代表性裂隙試驗比較進出漿濃度；觀察壓力升高是否伴隨流量降低和濾餅形成，再與水試的通水性分別判讀。檢查回漿是否富含細料。","textEn":"Check particle size and agglomeration in the mixed grout and compare inlet and outlet concentration in representative fracture tests. Observe pressure rise with declining flow and cake formation, keeping interpretation separate from water conductivity. Check whether returned grout is enriched in fines.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以顆粒尺寸與可灌性編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對實際混合漿液的粒徑與聚集狀態，用代表性裂隙試驗比較進出漿濃度；觀察壓力升高是否伴隨流量降低和濾餅形成，再與水試的通水性分別判讀。檢查回漿是否富含細料。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for particle size and groutability, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check particle size and agglomeration in the mixed grout and compare inlet and outlet concentration in representative fracture tests. Observe pressure rise with declining flow and cake formation, keeping interpretation separate from water conductivity. Check whether returned grout is enriched in fines.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Particle size and groutability\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對實際混合漿液的粒徑與聚集狀態，用代表性裂隙試驗比較進出漿濃度；觀察壓力升高是否伴隨流量降低和濾餅形成，再與水試的通水性分別判讀。","後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check particle size and agglomeration in the mixed grout and compare inlet and outlet concentration in representative fracture tests.","An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對實際混合漿液的粒徑與聚集狀態，用代表性裂隙試驗比較進出漿濃度；觀察壓力升高是否伴隨流量降低和濾餅形成，再與水試的通水性分別判讀。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check particle size and agglomeration in the mixed grout and compare inlet and outlet concentration in representative fracture tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b237-v15-08","title":"顆粒尺寸與可灌性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Particle size and groutability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Particle size and groutability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"細度證書不能代表混合後沒有團聚，孔口濾堵可能讓壓力上升卻沒有深部填充。若把高注入壓力當成帷幕密實證據，便可能掩蓋入口附近的局部封堵。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A fineness certificate does not exclude agglomeration after mixing. Entrance filtration can raise pressure without deep filling, so high injection pressure alone can conceal a locally blocked entrance rather than a continuous curtain. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若把高注入壓力當成帷幕密實證據，便可能掩蓋入口附近的局部封堵。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Entrance filtration can raise pressure without deep filling, so high injection pressure alone can conceal a locally blocked entrance rather than a continuous curtain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"細度證書不能代表混合後沒有團聚，孔口濾堵可能讓壓力上升卻沒有深部填充。若把高注入壓力當成帷幕密實證據，便可能掩蓋入口附近的局部封堵。","textEn":"A fineness certificate does not exclude agglomeration after mixing. Entrance filtration can raise pressure without deep filling, so high injection pressure alone can conceal a locally blocked entrance rather than a continuous curtain.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Particle size and groutability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。","細度證書不能代表混合後沒有團聚，孔口濾堵可能讓壓力上升卻沒有深部填充。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient.","A fineness certificate does not exclude agglomeration after mixing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"細度證書不能代表混合後沒有團聚，孔口濾堵可能讓壓力上升卻沒有深部填充。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A fineness certificate does not exclude agglomeration after mixing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b237-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「降伏應力與滲入距離」與「孔段壓力與水頭修正」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Yield stress and penetration length\" and \"Stage pressure and head correction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b237-v15-09","title":"降伏應力與滲入距離：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Yield stress and penetration length: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「降伏應力與滲入距離」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Yield stress and penetration length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"含顆粒漿液常有降伏應力，壓力梯度不足時不會像水一樣持續流動。平行裂隙中的門檻量級可解釋為何低黏度仍可能停止，但實際材料也有時變性。 假設Bingham漿降伏應力5 Pa、裂隙開度0.5 mm、長10 m，最低壓差尺度2τyL/b=200 kPa；理想平行板，非現地注入設定。 等待時間改變漿液結構，實際降伏值可能不同於初拌值；裂隙分叉和漏失也使壓力分配改變。只用泵表壓除距離，不能得到真正前緣壓力梯度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「降伏應力與滲入距離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Particle-bearing grout often has yield stress and will not flow like water below a sufficient pressure gradient. An ideal fracture threshold explains arrested penetration despite low plastic viscosity, with real materials also changing over time. Assume Bingham yield stress 5 Pa, aperture 0.5 mm and length 10 m. Threshold scale 2τyL/b=200 kPa, for ideal parallel plates and not a field injection setting. Waiting changes grout structure and yield stress, while branching and losses redistribute pressure. Pump gauge pressure divided by distance does not establish the actual gradient at the advancing front within the fracture network. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Yield stress and penetration length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Bingham漿降伏應力5 Pa、裂隙開度0.5 mm、長10 m，最低壓差尺度2τyL/b=200 kPa；理想平行板，非現地注入設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Bingham yield stress 5 Pa, aperture 0.5 mm and length 10 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「降伏應力與滲入距離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Yield stress and penetration length”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-09-k1","title":"降伏應力與滲入距離","titleEn":"Yield stress and penetration length","text":"含顆粒漿液常有降伏應力，壓力梯度不足時不會像水一樣持續流動。平行裂隙中的門檻量級可解釋為何低黏度仍可能停止，但實際材料也有時變性。","textEn":"Particle-bearing grout often has yield stress and will not flow like water below a sufficient pressure gradient. An ideal fracture threshold explains arrested penetration despite low plastic viscosity, with real materials also changing over time.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「降伏應力與滲入距離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Yield stress and penetration length\" is correct?","options":["含顆粒漿液常有降伏應力，壓力梯度不足時不會像水一樣持續流動。","漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。","泵端表壓可不經高程和地下水修正直接當成孔段有效壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Particle-bearing grout often has yield stress and will not flow like water below a sufficient pressure gradient.","Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient.","Pump gauge pressure directly equals effective stage pressure without elevation or groundwater correction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"含顆粒漿液常有降伏應力，壓力梯度不足時不會像水一樣持續流動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Particle-bearing grout often has yield stress and will not flow like water below a sufficient pressure gradient. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b237-v15-10","title":"降伏應力與滲入距離：定量估算","titleEn":"Yield stress and penetration length: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「降伏應力與滲入距離」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Yield stress and penetration length” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Bingham漿降伏應力5 Pa、裂隙開度0.5 mm、長10 m，最低壓差尺度2τyL/b=200 kPa；理想平行板，非現地注入設定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Bingham yield stress 5 Pa, aperture 0.5 mm and length 10 m. Threshold scale 2τyL/b=200 kPa, for ideal parallel plates and not a field injection setting. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以流變儀量測同齡期與溫度的降伏和塑性黏度，檢查剪切歷史影響；用裂隙模型比對停止前緣，並將材料凝結、濾堵與降伏造成的停流分開辨認。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure yield stress and plastic viscosity at matched age and temperature, checking shear history.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Bingham漿降伏應力5 Pa、裂隙開度0.5 mm、長10 m，最低壓差尺度2τyL/b=200 kPa；理想平行板，非現地注入設定。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Bingham yield stress 5 Pa, aperture 0.5 mm and length 10 m. Threshold scale 2τyL/b=200 kPa, for ideal parallel plates and not a field injection setting.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「降伏應力與滲入距離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Yield stress and penetration length\", which statement holds?","options":["供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Bingham漿降伏應力5 Pa、裂隙開度0.5 mm、長10 m，最低壓差尺度2τyL/b=200 kPa。","孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。"],"optionsEn":["Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Bingham yield stress 5 Pa, aperture 0.5 mm and length 10 m.","Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Bingham漿降伏應力5 Pa、裂隙開度0.5 mm、長10 m，最低壓差尺度2τyL/b=200 kPa；理想平行板，非現地注入設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume Bingham yield stress 5 Pa, aperture 0.5 mm and length 10 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b237-v15-11","title":"降伏應力與滲入距離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Yield stress and penetration length: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「降伏應力與滲入距離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Yield stress and penetration length” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以流變儀量測同齡期與溫度的降伏和塑性黏度，檢查剪切歷史影響；用裂隙模型比對停止前緣，並將材料凝結、濾堵與降伏造成的停流分開辨認。比較靜置後再剪切的反應。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure yield stress and plastic viscosity at matched age and temperature, checking shear history. Compare stopped fronts in fracture models and distinguish arrest caused by setting, filtration and yield behavior rather than assigning one cause automatically. Compare response after rest and renewed shearing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以降伏應力與滲入距離編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以流變儀量測同齡期與溫度的降伏和塑性黏度，檢查剪切歷史影響；用裂隙模型比對停止前緣，並將材料凝結、濾堵與降伏造成的停流分開辨認。比較靜置後再剪切的反應。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for yield stress and penetration length, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure yield stress and plastic viscosity at matched age and temperature, checking shear history. Compare stopped fronts in fracture models and distinguish arrest caused by setting, filtration and yield behavior rather than assigning one cause automatically. Compare response after rest and renewed shearing.","failure":"注意干擾：等待時間改變漿液結構，實際降伏值可能不同於初拌值；裂隙分叉和漏失也使壓力分配改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Waiting changes grout structure and yield stress, while branching and losses redistribute pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以流變儀量測同齡期與溫度的降伏和塑性黏度，檢查剪切歷史影響；用裂隙模型比對停止前緣，並將材料凝結、濾堵與降伏造成的停流分開辨認。比較靜置後再剪切的反應。","textEn":"Measure yield stress and plastic viscosity at matched age and temperature, checking shear history. Compare stopped fronts in fracture models and distinguish arrest caused by setting, filtration and yield behavior rather than assigning one cause automatically. Compare response after rest and renewed shearing.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以降伏應力與滲入距離編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以流變儀量測同齡期與溫度的降伏和塑性黏度，檢查剪切歷史影響；用裂隙模型比對停止前緣，並將材料凝結、濾堵與降伏造成的停流分開辨認。比較靜置後再剪切的反應。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for yield stress and penetration length, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure yield stress and plastic viscosity at matched age and temperature, checking shear history. Compare stopped fronts in fracture models and distinguish arrest caused by setting, filtration and yield behavior rather than assigning one cause automatically. Compare response after rest and renewed shearing.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「降伏應力與滲入距離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Yield stress and penetration length\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。","以流變儀量測同齡期與溫度的降伏和塑性黏度，檢查剪切歷史影響；用裂隙模型比對停止前緣，並將材料凝結、濾堵與降伏造成的停流分開辨認。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored.","Measure yield stress and plastic viscosity at matched age and temperature, checking shear history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以流變儀量測同齡期與溫度的降伏和塑性黏度，檢查剪切歷史影響；用裂隙模型比對停止前緣，並將材料凝結、濾堵與降伏造成的停流分開辨認。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure yield stress and plastic viscosity at matched age and temperature, checking shear history. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b237-v15-12","title":"降伏應力與滲入距離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Yield stress and penetration length: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「降伏應力與滲入距離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Yield stress and penetration length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"等待時間改變漿液結構，實際降伏值可能不同於初拌值；裂隙分叉和漏失也使壓力分配改變。只用泵表壓除距離，不能得到真正前緣壓力梯度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Waiting changes grout structure and yield stress, while branching and losses redistribute pressure. Pump gauge pressure divided by distance does not establish the actual gradient at the advancing front within the fracture network. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只用泵表壓除距離，不能得到真正前緣壓力梯度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pump gauge pressure divided by distance does not establish the actual gradient at the advancing front within the fracture network.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"等待時間改變漿液結構，實際降伏值可能不同於初拌值；裂隙分叉和漏失也使壓力分配改變。只用泵表壓除距離，不能得到真正前緣壓力梯度。","textEn":"Waiting changes grout structure and yield stress, while branching and losses redistribute pressure. Pump gauge pressure divided by distance does not establish the actual gradient at the advancing front within the fracture network.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「降伏應力與滲入距離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Yield stress and penetration length\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["等待時間改變漿液結構，實際降伏值可能不同於初拌值；裂隙分叉和漏失也使壓力分配改變。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","泵端表壓可不經高程和地下水修正直接當成孔段有效壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Waiting changes grout structure and yield stress, while branching and losses redistribute pressure.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Pump gauge pressure directly equals effective stage pressure without elevation or groundwater correction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"等待時間改變漿液結構，實際降伏值可能不同於初拌值；裂隙分叉和漏失也使壓力分配改變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Waiting changes grout structure and yield stress, while branching and losses redistribute pressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b237-v15-13","title":"孔段壓力與水頭修正：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stage pressure and head correction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「孔段壓力與水頭修正」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stage pressure and head correction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"泵端壓力經過管路損失與高程差後才成為孔段壓力，再扣地下水壓得到驅動差。把表壓直接當岩體有效注入壓，會混淆量測位置與參考基準。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設表壓500 kPa、下行漿柱20 m且密度1500 kg/m³、管損50 kPa、地下水壓200 kPa，有效差544.3 kPa；靜態高程修正示例。 管損隨流量改變，停泵讀值不能直接代表注入時孔段壓力。高程方向若用錯符號會產生巨大偏差，還可能把地下水自然壓力誤算為注入效果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔段壓力與水頭修正」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pump pressure changes through line loss and elevation before reaching the test stage. Subtracting groundwater pressure gives the driving difference, so gauge readings cannot directly represent effective injection pressure in the rock. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume gauge pressure 500 kPa, twenty-metre descending grout column at 1500 kg/m³, line loss 50 kPa and groundwater pressure 200 kPa. Effective difference is 544.3 kPa, a head-correction example. Line losses vary with flow, so stopped-pump readings do not represent flowing stage pressure. A wrong elevation sign creates large error and can confuse natural groundwater pressure with injection-driven response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stage pressure and head correction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「泵端表壓可不經高程和地下水修正直接當成孔段有效壓力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Pump gauge pressure directly equals effective stage pressure without elevation or groundwater correction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔段壓力與水頭修正」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stage pressure and head correction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-13-k1","title":"孔段壓力與水頭修正","titleEn":"Stage pressure and head correction","text":"泵端壓力經過管路損失與高程差後才成為孔段壓力，再扣地下水壓得到驅動差。把表壓直接當岩體有效注入壓，會混淆量測位置與參考基準。","textEn":"Pump pressure changes through line loss and elevation before reaching the test stage. Subtracting groundwater pressure gives the driving difference, so gauge readings cannot directly represent effective injection pressure in the rock.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：泵端表壓可不經高程和地下水修正直接當成孔段有效壓力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Pump gauge pressure directly equals effective stage pressure without elevation or groundwater correction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔段壓力與水頭修正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stage pressure and head correction\" is correct?","options":["泵端表壓可不經高程和地下水修正直接當成孔段有效壓力。","泵端壓力經過管路損失與高程差後才成為孔段壓力，再扣地下水壓得到驅動差。","吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。"],"optionsEn":["Pump gauge pressure directly equals effective stage pressure without elevation or groundwater correction.","Pump pressure changes through line loss and elevation before reaching the test stage.","A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"泵端壓力經過管路損失與高程差後才成為孔段壓力，再扣地下水壓得到驅動差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pump pressure changes through line loss and elevation before reaching the test stage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b237-v15-14","title":"孔段壓力與水頭修正：定量估算","titleEn":"Stage pressure and head correction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔段壓力與水頭修正」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stage pressure and head correction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設表壓500 kPa、下行漿柱20 m且密度1500 kg/m³、管損50 kPa、地下水壓200 kPa，有效差544.3 kPa；靜態高程修正示例。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume gauge pressure 500 kPa, twenty-metre descending grout column at 1500 kg/m³, line loss 50 kPa and groundwater pressure 200 kPa. Effective difference is 544.3 kPa, a head-correction example. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：記錄壓力計與孔段高程、漿密度及流量，獨立估算管損後對照孔內量測；停流和流動狀態分別核對，確認符號和表壓零點未隨設備移動而混淆。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record gauge and stage elevations, grout density and flow, comparing corrected estimates with downhole measurement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設表壓500 kPa、下行漿柱20 m且密度1500 kg/m³、管損50 kPa、地下水壓200 kPa，有效差544.3 kPa；靜態高程修正示例。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume gauge pressure 500 kPa, twenty-metre descending grout column at 1500 kg/m³, line loss 50 kPa and groundwater pressure 200 kPa. Effective difference is 544.3 kPa, a head-correction example.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔段壓力與水頭修正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stage pressure and head correction\", which statement holds?","options":["標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。","後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。"],"optionsEn":["Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions.","An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b237-v15-15","title":"孔段壓力與水頭修正：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stage pressure and head correction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔段壓力與水頭修正」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stage pressure and head correction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"記錄壓力計與孔段高程、漿密度及流量，獨立估算管損後對照孔內量測；停流和流動狀態分別核對，確認符號和表壓零點未隨設備移動而混淆。以靜止漿柱作零流量對照。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record gauge and stage elevations, grout density and flow, comparing corrected estimates with downhole measurement. Check flowing and stopped conditions separately and verify signs and gauge zero after equipment relocation. Use a stationary grout column as a zero-flow comparison. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以孔段壓力與水頭修正編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。記錄壓力計與孔段高程、漿密度及流量，獨立估算管損後對照孔內量測；停流和流動狀態分別核對，確認符號和表壓零點未隨設備移動而混淆。以靜止漿柱作零流量對照。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for stage pressure and head correction, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Record gauge and stage elevations, grout density and flow, comparing corrected estimates with downhole measurement. Check flowing and stopped conditions separately and verify signs and gauge zero after equipment relocation. Use a stationary grout column as a zero-flow comparison.","failure":"注意干擾：管損隨流量改變，停泵讀值不能直接代表注入時孔段壓力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Line losses vary with flow, so stopped-pump readings do not represent flowing stage pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"記錄壓力計與孔段高程、漿密度及流量，獨立估算管損後對照孔內量測；停流和流動狀態分別核對，確認符號和表壓零點未隨設備移動而混淆。以靜止漿柱作零流量對照。","textEn":"Record gauge and stage elevations, grout density and flow, comparing corrected estimates with downhole measurement. Check flowing and stopped conditions separately and verify signs and gauge zero after equipment relocation. Use a stationary grout column as a zero-flow comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以孔段壓力與水頭修正編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。記錄壓力計與孔段高程、漿密度及流量，獨立估算管損後對照孔內量測；停流和流動狀態分別核對，確認符號和表壓零點未隨設備移動而混淆。以靜止漿柱作零流量對照。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for stage pressure and head correction, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Record gauge and stage elevations, grout density and flow, comparing corrected estimates with downhole measurement. Check flowing and stopped conditions separately and verify signs and gauge zero after equipment relocation. Use a stationary grout column as a zero-flow comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔段壓力與水頭修正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stage pressure and head correction\"?","options":["記錄壓力計與孔段高程、漿密度及流量，獨立估算管損後對照孔內量測；停流和流動狀態分別核對，確認符號和表壓零點未隨設備移動而混淆。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。"],"optionsEn":["Record gauge and stage elevations, grout density and flow, comparing corrected estimates with downhole measurement.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture."],"answer":0,"explanation":"記錄壓力計與孔段高程、漿密度及流量，獨立估算管損後對照孔內量測；停流和流動狀態分別核對，確認符號和表壓零點未隨設備移動而混淆。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record gauge and stage elevations, grout density and flow, comparing corrected estimates with downhole measurement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b237-v15-16","title":"孔段壓力與水頭修正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stage pressure and head correction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔段壓力與水頭修正」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stage pressure and head correction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"管損隨流量改變，停泵讀值不能直接代表注入時孔段壓力。高程方向若用錯符號會產生巨大偏差，還可能把地下水自然壓力誤算為注入效果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Line losses vary with flow, so stopped-pump readings do not represent flowing stage pressure. A wrong elevation sign creates large error and can confuse natural groundwater pressure with injection-driven response. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：高程方向若用錯符號會產生巨大偏差，還可能把地下水自然壓力誤算為注入效果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A wrong elevation sign creates large error and can confuse natural groundwater pressure with injection-driven response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「泵端表壓可不經高程和地下水修正直接當成孔段有效壓力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Pump gauge pressure directly equals effective stage pressure without elevation or groundwater correction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"管損隨流量改變，停泵讀值不能直接代表注入時孔段壓力。高程方向若用錯符號會產生巨大偏差，還可能把地下水自然壓力誤算為注入效果。","textEn":"Line losses vary with flow, so stopped-pump readings do not represent flowing stage pressure. A wrong elevation sign creates large error and can confuse natural groundwater pressure with injection-driven response.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔段壓力與水頭修正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stage pressure and head correction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","管損隨流量改變，停泵讀值不能直接代表注入時孔段壓力。","吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Line losses vary with flow, so stopped-pump readings do not represent flowing stage pressure.","A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"管損隨流量改變，停泵讀值不能直接代表注入時孔段壓力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Line losses vary with flow, so stopped-pump readings do not represent flowing stage pressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b237-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」與「耗漿量與孔隙估算」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries\" and \"Grout take and void estimate\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b237-v15-17","title":"岩體抬動與壓力邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rock jacking and pressure boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"注入壓力若推開節理會改變岩體結構，吸漿量增加不一定代表成功填充。抬動應與原位應力、覆蓋及孔壓共同判讀，不能由固定深度比例推定全部條件。 假設某面總正應力600 kPa、原孔壓200 kPa，有效壓縮400 kPa；若額外孔壓升300 kPa，剩100 kPa，忽略黏結與三維應力重分配。 高壓造成新通道可能短期增加吸漿量，卻把漿液帶到非目標區。若只追求耗漿量而不查抬動和回流，可能損害既有接觸或鄰近構造。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Injection can open joints and change rock structure, so increased take is not automatically successful filling. Jacking interpretation requires in-situ stress, cover and pore pressure rather than one universal depth rule. Assume joint total normal stress 600 kPa and initial pore pressure 200 kPa, leaving effective compression 400 kPa. Added pressure 300 kPa leaves 100 kPa, excluding bond and three-dimensional redistribution. Pressure-created paths can increase take while diverting grout away from its target. Pursuing consumption without checking movement and returns can damage existing contacts or adjacent structures instead of improving the intended barrier. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rock jacking and pressure boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設某面總正應力600 kPa、原孔壓200 kPa，有效壓縮400 kPa；若額外孔壓升300 kPa，剩100 kPa，忽略黏結與三維應力重分配。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint total normal stress 600 kPa and initial pore pressure 200 kPa, leaving effective compression 400 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rock jacking and pressure boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-17-k1","title":"岩體抬動與壓力邊界","titleEn":"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries","text":"注入壓力若推開節理會改變岩體結構，吸漿量增加不一定代表成功填充。抬動應與原位應力、覆蓋及孔壓共同判讀，不能由固定深度比例推定全部條件。","textEn":"Injection can open joints and change rock structure, so increased take is not automatically successful filling. Jacking interpretation requires in-situ stress, cover and pore pressure rather than one universal depth rule.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries\" is correct?","options":["吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。","供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。","注入壓力若推開節理會改變岩體結構，吸漿量增加不一定代表成功填充。"],"optionsEn":["A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling.","Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures.","Injection can open joints and change rock structure, so increased take is not automatically successful filling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"注入壓力若推開節理會改變岩體結構，吸漿量增加不一定代表成功填充。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Injection can open joints and change rock structure, so increased take is not automatically successful filling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b237-v15-18","title":"岩體抬動與壓力邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rock jacking and pressure boundaries” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設某面總正應力600 kPa、原孔壓200 kPa，有效壓縮400 kPa；若額外孔壓升300 kPa，剩100 kPa，忽略黏結與三維應力重分配。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint total normal stress 600 kPa and initial pore pressure 200 kPa, leaving effective compression 400 kPa. Added pressure 300 kPa leaves 100 kPa, excluding bond and three-dimensional redistribution. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測孔壓、表面抬動和鄰孔回應，檢查壓流曲線突變是否伴隨幾何改變；以獨立水準基準排除儀器漂移，將可逆壓縮和不可逆張開分開記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure pore pressure, uplift and neighboring-hole response synchronously and test whether pressure-flow breaks accompany movement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設某面總正應力600 kPa、原孔壓200 kPa，有效壓縮400 kPa；若額外孔壓升300 kPa，剩100 kPa，忽略黏結與三維應力重分配。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint total normal stress 600 kPa and initial pore pressure 200 kPa, leaving effective compression 400 kPa. Added pressure 300 kPa leaves 100 kPa, excluding bond and three-dimensional redistribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設某面總正應力600 kPa、原孔壓200 kPa，有效壓縮400 kPa。","孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。","驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint total normal stress 600 kPa and initial pore pressure 200 kPa, leaving effective compression 400 kPa.","Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth.","A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設某面總正應力600 kPa、原孔壓200 kPa，有效壓縮400 kPa；若額外孔壓升300 kPa，剩100 kPa，忽略黏結與三維應力重分配。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint total normal stress 600 kPa and initial pore pressure 200 kPa, leaving effective compression 400 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b237-v15-19","title":"岩體抬動與壓力邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rock jacking and pressure boundaries” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測孔壓、表面抬動和鄰孔回應，檢查壓流曲線突變是否伴隨幾何改變；以獨立水準基準排除儀器漂移，將可逆壓縮和不可逆張開分開記錄。記錄遠離孔口的參考點位移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure pore pressure, uplift and neighboring-hole response synchronously and test whether pressure-flow breaks accompany movement. Use an independent leveling reference to exclude drift and distinguish reversible deformation from irreversible opening. Record movement at reference points away from the hole. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以岩體抬動與壓力邊界編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步量測孔壓、表面抬動和鄰孔回應，檢查壓流曲線突變是否伴隨幾何改變；以獨立水準基準排除儀器漂移，將可逆壓縮和不可逆張開分開記錄。記錄遠離孔口的參考點位移。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rock jacking and pressure boundaries, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure pore pressure, uplift and neighboring-hole response synchronously and test whether pressure-flow breaks accompany movement. Use an independent leveling reference to exclude drift and distinguish reversible deformation from irreversible opening. Record movement at reference points away from the hole.","failure":"注意干擾：高壓造成新通道可能短期增加吸漿量，卻把漿液帶到非目標區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Pressure-created paths can increase take while diverting grout away from its target. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測孔壓、表面抬動和鄰孔回應，檢查壓流曲線突變是否伴隨幾何改變；以獨立水準基準排除儀器漂移，將可逆壓縮和不可逆張開分開記錄。記錄遠離孔口的參考點位移。","textEn":"Measure pore pressure, uplift and neighboring-hole response synchronously and test whether pressure-flow breaks accompany movement. Use an independent leveling reference to exclude drift and distinguish reversible deformation from irreversible opening. Record movement at reference points away from the hole.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以岩體抬動與壓力邊界編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步量測孔壓、表面抬動和鄰孔回應，檢查壓流曲線突變是否伴隨幾何改變；以獨立水準基準排除儀器漂移，將可逆壓縮和不可逆張開分開記錄。記錄遠離孔口的參考點位移。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rock jacking and pressure boundaries, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure pore pressure, uplift and neighboring-hole response synchronously and test whether pressure-flow breaks accompany movement. Use an independent leveling reference to exclude drift and distinguish reversible deformation from irreversible opening. Record movement at reference points away from the hole.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","同步量測孔壓、表面抬動和鄰孔回應，檢查壓流曲線突變是否伴隨幾何改變；以獨立水準基準排除儀器漂移，將可逆壓縮和不可逆張開分開記錄。","只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure pore pressure, uplift and neighboring-hole response synchronously and test whether pressure-flow breaks accompany movement.","Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步量測孔壓、表面抬動和鄰孔回應，檢查壓流曲線突變是否伴隨幾何改變；以獨立水準基準排除儀器漂移，將可逆壓縮和不可逆張開分開記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure pore pressure, uplift and neighboring-hole response synchronously and test whether pressure-flow breaks accompany movement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b237-v15-20","title":"岩體抬動與壓力邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rock jacking and pressure boundaries” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高壓造成新通道可能短期增加吸漿量，卻把漿液帶到非目標區。若只追求耗漿量而不查抬動和回流，可能損害既有接觸或鄰近構造。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Pressure-created paths can increase take while diverting grout away from its target. Pursuing consumption without checking movement and returns can damage existing contacts or adjacent structures instead of improving the intended barrier. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只追求耗漿量而不查抬動和回流，可能損害既有接觸或鄰近構造。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pursuing consumption without checking movement and returns can damage existing contacts or adjacent structures instead of improving the intended barrier.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高壓造成新通道可能短期增加吸漿量，卻把漿液帶到非目標區。若只追求耗漿量而不查抬動和回流，可能損害既有接觸或鄰近構造。","textEn":"Pressure-created paths can increase take while diverting grout away from its target. Pursuing consumption without checking movement and returns can damage existing contacts or adjacent structures instead of improving the intended barrier.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rock jacking and pressure boundaries\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。","高壓造成新通道可能短期增加吸漿量，卻把漿液帶到非目標區。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures.","Pressure-created paths can increase take while diverting grout away from its target."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高壓造成新通道可能短期增加吸漿量，卻把漿液帶到非目標區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Pressure-created paths can increase take while diverting grout away from its target. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b237-v15-21","title":"耗漿量與孔隙估算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Grout take and void estimate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「耗漿量與孔隙估算」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grout take and void estimate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"耗漿量包含管內存量、回流、漏失和實際填充，不能全當成岩體孔隙。帷幕幾何的等效孔隙估算可做量級比較，但裂隙分布通常高度不均。 假設處理區100×20×3 m、等效可填孔隙率0.01，理想填充60 m³；實際供漿90 m³與其差30 m³須分解來源，非自動灌得更好。 漿液流入大空洞或遠端通道會消耗大量材料而不形成連續帷幕，析水又使硬化體積小於注入體積。總耗漿相符仍不能證明目標裂隙全部被封住。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「耗漿量與孔隙估算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Grout consumption includes line storage, returns, losses and actual filling. A geometric equivalent-void estimate compares scales, but fracture distribution is usually uneven and consumption cannot all be assigned to rock voids. Assume treatment zone 100×20×3 m with equivalent fillable void fraction 0.01. Ideal volume is 60 m³; delivery 90 m³ leaves 30 m³ requiring source accounting rather than proving improvement. A cavity or distant channel consumes material without forming a continuous curtain, while bleeding reduces hardened volume. Matching total take therefore does not prove that all targeted flow paths have been sealed. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grout take and void estimate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設處理區100×20×3 m、等效可填孔隙率0.01，理想填充60 m³；實際供漿90 m³與其差30 m³須分解來源，非自動灌得更好。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume treatment zone 100×20×3 m with equivalent fillable void fraction 0.01.","failure":"常見誤解：「供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「耗漿量與孔隙估算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grout take and void estimate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-21-k1","title":"耗漿量與孔隙估算","titleEn":"Grout take and void estimate","text":"耗漿量包含管內存量、回流、漏失和實際填充，不能全當成岩體孔隙。帷幕幾何的等效孔隙估算可做量級比較，但裂隙分布通常高度不均。","textEn":"Grout consumption includes line storage, returns, losses and actual filling. A geometric equivalent-void estimate compares scales, but fracture distribution is usually uneven and consumption cannot all be assigned to rock voids.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「耗漿量與孔隙估算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Grout take and void estimate\" is correct?","options":["耗漿量包含管內存量、回流、漏失和實際填充，不能全當成岩體孔隙。","供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。","標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。"],"optionsEn":["Grout consumption includes line storage, returns, losses and actual filling.","Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures.","Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"耗漿量包含管內存量、回流、漏失和實際填充，不能全當成岩體孔隙。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Grout consumption includes line storage, returns, losses and actual filling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b237-v15-22","title":"耗漿量與孔隙估算：定量估算","titleEn":"Grout take and void estimate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「耗漿量與孔隙估算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grout take and void estimate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設處理區100×20×3 m、等效可填孔隙率0.01，理想填充60 m³；實際供漿90 m³與其差30 m³須分解來源，非自動灌得更好。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume treatment zone 100×20×3 m with equivalent fillable void fraction 0.01. Ideal volume is 60 m³; delivery 90 m³ leaves 30 m³ requiring source accounting rather than proving improvement. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立供漿、回流、設備存量與地表逸出分帳，逐孔段核對體積和固體質量；把耗漿分布與地質裂隙對照，檢查極大值是否由單一通道控制而非平均孔隙增加。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Account separately for supply, returns, equipment storage and surface escape, checking volume and solids by stage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設處理區100×20×3 m、等效可填孔隙率0.01，理想填充60 m³；實際供漿90 m³與其差30 m³須分解來源，非自動灌得更好。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume treatment zone 100×20×3 m with equivalent fillable void fraction 0.01. Ideal volume is 60 m³; delivery 90 m³ leaves 30 m³ requiring source accounting rather than proving improvement.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「耗漿量與孔隙估算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Grout take and void estimate\", which statement holds?","options":["後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設處理區100×20×3 m、等效可填孔隙率0.01，理想填充60 m³。","水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。"],"optionsEn":["An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume treatment zone 100×20×3 m with equivalent fillable void fraction 0.01.","Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設處理區100×20×3 m、等效可填孔隙率0.01，理想填充60 m³；實際供漿90 m³與其差30 m³須分解來源，非自動灌得更好。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume treatment zone 100×20×3 m with equivalent fillable void fraction 0.01. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b237-v15-23","title":"耗漿量與孔隙估算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Grout take and void estimate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「耗漿量與孔隙估算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grout take and void estimate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立供漿、回流、設備存量與地表逸出分帳，逐孔段核對體積和固體質量；把耗漿分布與地質裂隙對照，檢查極大值是否由單一通道控制而非平均孔隙增加。比較重量與體積計量的一致性。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Account separately for supply, returns, equipment storage and surface escape, checking volume and solids by stage. Compare takes with mapped fractures and determine whether extreme values reflect one channel rather than uniformly increased voids. Cross-check mass-based and volume-based accounting. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以耗漿量與孔隙估算編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。建立供漿、回流、設備存量與地表逸出分帳，逐孔段核對體積和固體質量；把耗漿分布與地質裂隙對照，檢查極大值是否由單一通道控制而非平均孔隙增加。比較重量與體積計量的一致性。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for grout take and void estimate, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Account separately for supply, returns, equipment storage and surface escape, checking volume and solids by stage. Compare takes with mapped fractures and determine whether extreme values reflect one channel rather than uniformly increased voids. Cross-check mass-based and volume-based accounting.","failure":"注意干擾：漿液流入大空洞或遠端通道會消耗大量材料而不形成連續帷幕，析水又使硬化體積小於注入體積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A cavity or distant channel consumes material without forming a continuous curtain, while bleeding reduces hardened volume. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立供漿、回流、設備存量與地表逸出分帳，逐孔段核對體積和固體質量；把耗漿分布與地質裂隙對照，檢查極大值是否由單一通道控制而非平均孔隙增加。比較重量與體積計量的一致性。","textEn":"Account separately for supply, returns, equipment storage and surface escape, checking volume and solids by stage. Compare takes with mapped fractures and determine whether extreme values reflect one channel rather than uniformly increased voids. Cross-check mass-based and volume-based accounting.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以耗漿量與孔隙估算編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。建立供漿、回流、設備存量與地表逸出分帳，逐孔段核對體積和固體質量；把耗漿分布與地質裂隙對照，檢查極大值是否由單一通道控制而非平均孔隙增加。比較重量與體積計量的一致性。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for grout take and void estimate, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Account separately for supply, returns, equipment storage and surface escape, checking volume and solids by stage. Compare takes with mapped fractures and determine whether extreme values reflect one channel rather than uniformly increased voids. Cross-check mass-based and volume-based accounting.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「耗漿量與孔隙估算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Grout take and void estimate\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。","建立供漿、回流、設備存量與地表逸出分帳，逐孔段核對體積和固體質量；把耗漿分布與地質裂隙對照，檢查極大值是否由單一通道控制而非平均孔隙增加。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient.","Account separately for supply, returns, equipment storage and surface escape, checking volume and solids by stage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立供漿、回流、設備存量與地表逸出分帳，逐孔段核對體積和固體質量；把耗漿分布與地質裂隙對照，檢查極大值是否由單一通道控制而非平均孔隙增加。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Account separately for supply, returns, equipment storage and surface escape, checking volume and solids by stage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b237-v15-24","title":"耗漿量與孔隙估算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Grout take and void estimate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「耗漿量與孔隙估算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grout take and void estimate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漿液流入大空洞或遠端通道會消耗大量材料而不形成連續帷幕，析水又使硬化體積小於注入體積。總耗漿相符仍不能證明目標裂隙全部被封住。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A cavity or distant channel consumes material without forming a continuous curtain, while bleeding reduces hardened volume. Matching total take therefore does not prove that all targeted flow paths have been sealed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：總耗漿相符仍不能證明目標裂隙全部被封住。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Matching total take therefore does not prove that all targeted flow paths have been sealed.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漿液流入大空洞或遠端通道會消耗大量材料而不形成連續帷幕，析水又使硬化體積小於注入體積。總耗漿相符仍不能證明目標裂隙全部被封住。","textEn":"A cavity or distant channel consumes material without forming a continuous curtain, while bleeding reduces hardened volume. Matching total take therefore does not prove that all targeted flow paths have been sealed.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「耗漿量與孔隙估算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Grout take and void estimate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漿液流入大空洞或遠端通道會消耗大量材料而不形成連續帷幕，析水又使硬化體積小於注入體積。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。"],"optionsEn":["A cavity or distant channel consumes material without forming a continuous curtain, while bleeding reduces hardened volume.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"漿液流入大空洞或遠端通道會消耗大量材料而不形成連續帷幕，析水又使硬化體積小於注入體積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A cavity or distant channel consumes material without forming a continuous curtain, while bleeding reduces hardened volume. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b237-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「壓水試驗標準化」與「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Water-test normalization\" and \"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b237-v15-25","title":"壓水試驗標準化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Water-test normalization: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「壓水試驗標準化」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Water-test normalization” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"孔段長度與試驗壓力不同時，流量需標準化才能初步比較。比例換算假設近似線性流動，裂隙張開或紊流會破壞這個關係。 假設流量10 L/min、孔段5 m、有效試壓0.8 MPa，線性換算到1 MPa為10/5×1/0.8=2.5 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數。 同樣標準化數值可能來自不同裂隙幾何和各向異性，不能直接換成唯一k值。封塞旁漏或孔壁損傷也會提高讀數，需用獨立證據區分。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓水試驗標準化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Different stage lengths and test pressures require normalized flow for preliminary comparison. Proportional scaling assumes nearly linear flow, which joint opening and turbulence can invalidate. Assume flow 10 L/min, stage length 5 m and effective pressure 0.8 MPa. Linear normalization to 1 MPa gives 2.5 L/(min·m), not a permeability coefficient directly. Equal normalized values can arise from different fracture geometries and anisotropy and do not determine a unique k. Packer bypass and drilling damage also raise readings and require separate evidence to distinguish. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water-test normalization” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設流量10 L/min、孔段5 m、有效試壓0.8 MPa，線性換算到1 MPa為10/5×1/0.8=2.5 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume flow 10 L/min, stage length 5 m and effective pressure 0.8 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓水試驗標準化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water-test normalization”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-25-k1","title":"壓水試驗標準化","titleEn":"Water-test normalization","text":"孔段長度與試驗壓力不同時，流量需標準化才能初步比較。比例換算假設近似線性流動，裂隙張開或紊流會破壞這個關係。","textEn":"Different stage lengths and test pressures require normalized flow for preliminary comparison. Proportional scaling assumes nearly linear flow, which joint opening and turbulence can invalidate.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓水試驗標準化」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Water-test normalization\" is correct?","options":["標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。","孔段長度與試驗壓力不同時，流量需標準化才能初步比較。","孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。"],"optionsEn":["Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions.","Different stage lengths and test pressures require normalized flow for preliminary comparison.","Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔段長度與試驗壓力不同時，流量需標準化才能初步比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Different stage lengths and test pressures require normalized flow for preliminary comparison. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b237-v15-26","title":"壓水試驗標準化：定量估算","titleEn":"Water-test normalization: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓水試驗標準化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Water-test normalization” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設流量10 L/min、孔段5 m、有效試壓0.8 MPa，線性換算到1 MPa為10/5×1/0.8=2.5 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume flow 10 L/min, stage length 5 m and effective pressure 0.8 MPa. Linear normalization to 1 MPa gives 2.5 L/(min·m), not a permeability coefficient directly. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對有效壓力、孔段長度與封塞密封，繪升降壓流量曲線測線性；只在相同流況下比較前後結果，並保留原始各級數據，避免標準化掩蓋遲滯或漏流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify effective pressure, stage length and packer seal and plot ascending and descending pressure-flow curves.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設流量10 L/min、孔段5 m、有效試壓0.8 MPa，線性換算到1 MPa為10/5×1/0.8=2.5 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume flow 10 L/min, stage length 5 m and effective pressure 0.8 MPa. Linear normalization to 1 MPa gives 2.5 L/(min·m), not a permeability coefficient directly.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓水試驗標準化」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Water-test normalization\", which statement holds?","options":["驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。","只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設流量10 L/min、孔段5 m、有效試壓0.8 MPa，線性換算到1 MPa為10/5×1/0.8=2.5 L/(min·m)。"],"optionsEn":["A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored.","Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume flow 10 L/min, stage length 5 m and effective pressure 0.8 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設流量10 L/min、孔段5 m、有效試壓0.8 MPa，線性換算到1 MPa為10/5×1/0.8=2.5 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume flow 10 L/min, stage length 5 m and effective pressure 0.8 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b237-v15-27","title":"壓水試驗標準化：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Water-test normalization: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓水試驗標準化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water-test normalization” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對有效壓力、孔段長度與封塞密封，繪升降壓流量曲線測線性；只在相同流況下比較前後結果，並保留原始各級數據，避免標準化掩蓋遲滯或漏流。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify effective pressure, stage length and packer seal and plot ascending and descending pressure-flow curves. Compare before and after only under equivalent regimes, retaining raw stages so normalization does not conceal hysteresis or leakage. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以壓水試驗標準化編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對有效壓力、孔段長度與封塞密封，繪升降壓流量曲線測線性；只在相同流況下比較前後結果，並保留原始各級數據，避免標準化掩蓋遲滯或漏流。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for water-test normalization, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Verify effective pressure, stage length and packer seal and plot ascending and descending pressure-flow curves. Compare before and after only under equivalent regimes, retaining raw stages so normalization does not conceal hysteresis or leakage.","failure":"注意干擾：同樣標準化數值可能來自不同裂隙幾何和各向異性，不能直接換成唯一k值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equal normalized values can arise from different fracture geometries and anisotropy and do not determine a unique k. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對有效壓力、孔段長度與封塞密封，繪升降壓流量曲線測線性；只在相同流況下比較前後結果，並保留原始各級數據，避免標準化掩蓋遲滯或漏流。","textEn":"Verify effective pressure, stage length and packer seal and plot ascending and descending pressure-flow curves. Compare before and after only under equivalent regimes, retaining raw stages so normalization does not conceal hysteresis or leakage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以壓水試驗標準化編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對有效壓力、孔段長度與封塞密封，繪升降壓流量曲線測線性；只在相同流況下比較前後結果，並保留原始各級數據，避免標準化掩蓋遲滯或漏流。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for water-test normalization, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Verify effective pressure, stage length and packer seal and plot ascending and descending pressure-flow curves. Compare before and after only under equivalent regimes, retaining raw stages so normalization does not conceal hysteresis or leakage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓水試驗標準化」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Water-test normalization\"?","options":["核對有效壓力、孔段長度與封塞密封，繪升降壓流量曲線測線性；只在相同流況下比較前後結果，並保留原始各級數據，避免標準化掩蓋遲滯或漏流。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","泵端表壓可不經高程和地下水修正直接當成孔段有效壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Verify effective pressure, stage length and packer seal and plot ascending and descending pressure-flow curves.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Pump gauge pressure directly equals effective stage pressure without elevation or groundwater correction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對有效壓力、孔段長度與封塞密封，繪升降壓流量曲線測線性；只在相同流況下比較前後結果，並保留原始各級數據，避免標準化掩蓋遲滯或漏流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify effective pressure, stage length and packer seal and plot ascending and descending pressure-flow curves. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b237-v15-28","title":"壓水試驗標準化：失效診斷","titleEn":"Water-test normalization: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓水試驗標準化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Water-test normalization” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同樣標準化數值可能來自不同裂隙幾何和各向異性，不能直接換成唯一k值。封塞旁漏或孔壁損傷也會提高讀數，需用獨立證據區分。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equal normalized values can arise from different fracture geometries and anisotropy and do not determine a unique k. Packer bypass and drilling damage also raise readings and require separate evidence to distinguish. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：封塞旁漏或孔壁損傷也會提高讀數，需用獨立證據區分。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Packer bypass and drilling damage also raise readings and require separate evidence to distinguish.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同樣標準化數值可能來自不同裂隙幾何和各向異性，不能直接換成唯一k值。封塞旁漏或孔壁損傷也會提高讀數，需用獨立證據區分。","textEn":"Equal normalized values can arise from different fracture geometries and anisotropy and do not determine a unique k. Packer bypass and drilling damage also raise readings and require separate evidence to distinguish.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓水試驗標準化」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Water-test normalization\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","同樣標準化數值可能來自不同裂隙幾何和各向異性，不能直接換成唯一k值。","孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Equal normalized values can arise from different fracture geometries and anisotropy and do not determine a unique k.","Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同樣標準化數值可能來自不同裂隙幾何和各向異性，不能直接換成唯一k值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equal normalized values can arise from different fracture geometries and anisotropy and do not determine a unique k. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b237-v15-29","title":"鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Borehole deviation and curtain continuity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"深孔會偏離設計線，孔口間距相符不代表深部間距相符。帷幕連續性依實際孔跡與可達處理範圍判讀，不能只按平面鑽孔圖驗收。 假設孔深60 m、固定偏斜角2°，水平偏移Lsin2°=2.094 m；直線偏孔示例，實際孔跡可能彎曲且方向變化。 兩孔朝相反方向偏移會在深部拉開大缺口，同向偏移則可能讓整排偏離目標。僅看平均偏斜角，會漏掉局部曲折造成的最近或最遠間距。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Deep holes deviate from design lines, so correct collar spacing does not establish spacing at depth. Curtain continuity depends on actual trajectories and treatment reach rather than the plan of drill collars alone. Assume hole length 60 m and constant deviation two degrees. Horizontal offset Lsin2°=2.094 m, a straight-deviation example rather than a curved real trajectory. Opposing deviations open deep gaps, while common-direction deviation shifts the row away from its target. Mean deviation angle misses local curvature controlling the closest and widest spacing between treatment paths. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Borehole deviation and curtain continuity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設孔深60 m、固定偏斜角2°，水平偏移Lsin2°=2.094 m；直線偏孔示例，實際孔跡可能彎曲且方向變化。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hole length 60 m and constant deviation two degrees.","failure":"常見誤解：「孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Borehole deviation and curtain continuity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-29-k1","title":"鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續","titleEn":"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity","text":"深孔會偏離設計線，孔口間距相符不代表深部間距相符。帷幕連續性依實際孔跡與可達處理範圍判讀，不能只按平面鑽孔圖驗收。","textEn":"Deep holes deviate from design lines, so correct collar spacing does not establish spacing at depth. Curtain continuity depends on actual trajectories and treatment reach rather than the plan of drill collars alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity\" is correct?","options":["孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。","後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。","深孔會偏離設計線，孔口間距相符不代表深部間距相符。"],"optionsEn":["Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth.","An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction.","Deep holes deviate from design lines, so correct collar spacing does not establish spacing at depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"深孔會偏離設計線，孔口間距相符不代表深部間距相符。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Deep holes deviate from design lines, so correct collar spacing does not establish spacing at depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b237-v15-30","title":"鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續：定量估算","titleEn":"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Borehole deviation and curtain continuity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設孔深60 m、固定偏斜角2°，水平偏移Lsin2°=2.094 m；直線偏孔示例，實際孔跡可能彎曲且方向變化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hole length 60 m and constant deviation two degrees. Horizontal offset Lsin2°=2.094 m, a straight-deviation example rather than a curved real trajectory. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用分段測斜重建三維孔跡，將相鄰孔在同高程的距離畫出；對照驗證孔與示蹤連通，檢查最大間隙位置，並保留磁性干擾和定位不確定度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconstruct three-dimensional paths with staged surveys and plot spacing between adjacent holes at equal elevations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設孔深60 m、固定偏斜角2°，水平偏移Lsin2°=2.094 m；直線偏孔示例，實際孔跡可能彎曲且方向變化。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hole length 60 m and constant deviation two degrees. Horizontal offset Lsin2°=2.094 m, a straight-deviation example rather than a curved real trajectory.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設孔深60 m、固定偏斜角2°，水平偏移Lsin2°=2.094 m；直線偏孔示例，實際孔跡可能彎曲且方向變化。","水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。","漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hole length 60 m and constant deviation two degrees.","Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture.","Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設孔深60 m、固定偏斜角2°，水平偏移Lsin2°=2.094 m；直線偏孔示例，實際孔跡可能彎曲且方向變化。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hole length 60 m and constant deviation two degrees. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b237-v15-31","title":"鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Borehole deviation and curtain continuity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用分段測斜重建三維孔跡，將相鄰孔在同高程的距離畫出；對照驗證孔與示蹤連通，檢查最大間隙位置，並保留磁性干擾和定位不確定度。將最大偏距位置納入覆蓋圖。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconstruct three-dimensional paths with staged surveys and plot spacing between adjacent holes at equal elevations. Compare verification holes and tracer connectivity, identifying largest gaps while retaining magnetic and positional uncertainties. Include maximum-deviation locations in the coverage map. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用分段測斜重建三維孔跡，將相鄰孔在同高程的距離畫出；對照驗證孔與示蹤連通，檢查最大間隙位置，並保留磁性干擾和定位不確定度。將最大偏距位置納入覆蓋圖。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for borehole deviation and curtain continuity, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Reconstruct three-dimensional paths with staged surveys and plot spacing between adjacent holes at equal elevations. Compare verification holes and tracer connectivity, identifying largest gaps while retaining magnetic and positional uncertainties. Include maximum-deviation locations in the coverage map.","failure":"注意干擾：兩孔朝相反方向偏移會在深部拉開大缺口，同向偏移則可能讓整排偏離目標。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Opposing deviations open deep gaps, while common-direction deviation shifts the row away from its target. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用分段測斜重建三維孔跡，將相鄰孔在同高程的距離畫出；對照驗證孔與示蹤連通，檢查最大間隙位置，並保留磁性干擾和定位不確定度。將最大偏距位置納入覆蓋圖。","textEn":"Reconstruct three-dimensional paths with staged surveys and plot spacing between adjacent holes at equal elevations. Compare verification holes and tracer connectivity, identifying largest gaps while retaining magnetic and positional uncertainties. Include maximum-deviation locations in the coverage map.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用分段測斜重建三維孔跡，將相鄰孔在同高程的距離畫出；對照驗證孔與示蹤連通，檢查最大間隙位置，並保留磁性干擾和定位不確定度。將最大偏距位置納入覆蓋圖。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for borehole deviation and curtain continuity, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Reconstruct three-dimensional paths with staged surveys and plot spacing between adjacent holes at equal elevations. Compare verification holes and tracer connectivity, identifying largest gaps while retaining magnetic and positional uncertainties. Include maximum-deviation locations in the coverage map.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用分段測斜重建三維孔跡，將相鄰孔在同高程的距離畫出；對照驗證孔與示蹤連通，檢查最大間隙位置，並保留磁性干擾和定位不確定度。","吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Reconstruct three-dimensional paths with staged surveys and plot spacing between adjacent holes at equal elevations.","A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用分段測斜重建三維孔跡，將相鄰孔在同高程的距離畫出；對照驗證孔與示蹤連通，檢查最大間隙位置，並保留磁性干擾和定位不確定度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconstruct three-dimensional paths with staged surveys and plot spacing between adjacent holes at equal elevations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b237-v15-32","title":"鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續：失效診斷","titleEn":"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Borehole deviation and curtain continuity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩孔朝相反方向偏移會在深部拉開大缺口，同向偏移則可能讓整排偏離目標。僅看平均偏斜角，會漏掉局部曲折造成的最近或最遠間距。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Opposing deviations open deep gaps, while common-direction deviation shifts the row away from its target. Mean deviation angle misses local curvature controlling the closest and widest spacing between treatment paths. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：僅看平均偏斜角，會漏掉局部曲折造成的最近或最遠間距。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean deviation angle misses local curvature controlling the closest and widest spacing between treatment paths.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩孔朝相反方向偏移會在深部拉開大缺口，同向偏移則可能讓整排偏離目標。僅看平均偏斜角，會漏掉局部曲折造成的最近或最遠間距。","textEn":"Opposing deviations open deep gaps, while common-direction deviation shifts the row away from its target. Mean deviation angle misses local curvature controlling the closest and widest spacing between treatment paths.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Borehole deviation and curtain continuity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。","兩孔朝相反方向偏移會在深部拉開大缺口，同向偏移則可能讓整排偏離目標。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction.","Opposing deviations open deep gaps, while common-direction deviation shifts the row away from its target."],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩孔朝相反方向偏移會在深部拉開大缺口，同向偏移則可能讓整排偏離目標。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Opposing deviations open deep gaps, while common-direction deviation shifts the row away from its target. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b237-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「序列孔耗量趨勢」與「獨立驗證與統計分布」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Successive-hole take trends\" and \"Independent verification and distributions\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b237-v15-33","title":"序列孔耗量趨勢：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Successive-hole take trends: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「序列孔耗量趨勢」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Successive-hole take trends” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"逐次縮小孔距常用來觀察處理後剩餘可灌性，但耗量下降也可能受材料、壓力和孔段條件改變。趨勢必須在可比較條件下解讀，不能單獨作完成證明。 假設可比較孔段的單位耗量由30降至12再到6 kg/m，最後相對初始下降80%；只是趨勢指標，不等同滲透率下降80%。 先前孔堵住入口會使後續孔吸漿少，卻可能留下更遠通道；濃漿用量的重量與稀漿體積也不可直接比較。只追求下降曲線會導致錯誤完工判讀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「序列孔耗量趨勢」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Successive spacing reduction can reveal remaining groutability, but declining take also reflects changed mixtures, pressures and stages. Trends require comparable conditions and cannot alone establish completion of a hydraulic barrier. Assume comparable unit takes fall from 30 to 12 to 6 kg/m. Final take is eighty percent below initial, a trend indicator rather than an eighty-percent permeability reduction. Earlier entrance blockage lowers later take while leaving distant paths, and dense-grout mass cannot directly compare with dilute-grout volume. Pursuing a falling curve alone can therefore lead to an incorrect completion assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Successive-hole take trends” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設可比較孔段的單位耗量由30降至12再到6 kg/m，最後相對初始下降80%；只是趨勢指標，不等同滲透率下降80%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume comparable unit takes fall from 30 to 12 to 6 kg/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「序列孔耗量趨勢」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Successive-hole take trends”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-33-k1","title":"序列孔耗量趨勢","titleEn":"Successive-hole take trends","text":"逐次縮小孔距常用來觀察處理後剩餘可灌性，但耗量下降也可能受材料、壓力和孔段條件改變。趨勢必須在可比較條件下解讀，不能單獨作完成證明。","textEn":"Successive spacing reduction can reveal remaining groutability, but declining take also reflects changed mixtures, pressures and stages. Trends require comparable conditions and cannot alone establish completion of a hydraulic barrier.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「序列孔耗量趨勢」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Successive-hole take trends\" is correct?","options":["逐次縮小孔距常用來觀察處理後剩餘可灌性，但耗量下降也可能受材料、壓力和孔段條件改變。","後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。","驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。"],"optionsEn":["Successive spacing reduction can reveal remaining groutability, but declining take also reflects changed mixtures, pressures and stages.","An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction.","A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐次縮小孔距常用來觀察處理後剩餘可灌性，但耗量下降也可能受材料、壓力和孔段條件改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Successive spacing reduction can reveal remaining groutability, but declining take also reflects changed mixtures, pressures and stages. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b237-v15-34","title":"序列孔耗量趨勢：定量估算","titleEn":"Successive-hole take trends: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「序列孔耗量趨勢」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Successive-hole take trends” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設可比較孔段的單位耗量由30降至12再到6 kg/m，最後相對初始下降80%；只是趨勢指標，不等同滲透率下降80%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume comparable unit takes fall from 30 to 12 to 6 kg/m. Final take is eighty percent below initial, a trend indicator rather than an eighty-percent permeability reduction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按相同地層、孔段長度和有效壓力分組比較耗量，核對材料濃度與停止條件；用獨立壓水或驗證孔檢查低耗量區仍否存在未被相交的連通裂隙。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Group takes by geology, stage length and effective pressure, checking mix concentration and stopping conditions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設可比較孔段的單位耗量由30降至12再到6 kg/m，最後相對初始下降80%；只是趨勢指標，不等同滲透率下降80%。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume comparable unit takes fall from 30 to 12 to 6 kg/m. Final take is eighty percent below initial, a trend indicator rather than an eighty-percent permeability reduction.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「序列孔耗量趨勢」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Successive-hole take trends\", which statement holds?","options":["只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設可比較孔段的單位耗量由30降至12再到6 kg/m，最後相對初始下降80%；只是趨勢指標，不等同滲透率下降80%。","泵端表壓可不經高程和地下水修正直接當成孔段有效壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume comparable unit takes fall from 30 to 12 to 6 kg/m.","Pump gauge pressure directly equals effective stage pressure without elevation or groundwater correction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設可比較孔段的單位耗量由30降至12再到6 kg/m，最後相對初始下降80%；只是趨勢指標，不等同滲透率下降80%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume comparable unit takes fall from 30 to 12 to 6 kg/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b237-v15-35","title":"序列孔耗量趨勢：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Successive-hole take trends: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「序列孔耗量趨勢」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Successive-hole take trends” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按相同地層、孔段長度和有效壓力分組比較耗量，核對材料濃度與停止條件；用獨立壓水或驗證孔檢查低耗量區仍否存在未被相交的連通裂隙。分開比較不同材料批次的結果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Group takes by geology, stage length and effective pressure, checking mix concentration and stopping conditions. Use independent water tests or verification holes to determine whether low-take regions retain connected fractures not intersected by treatment. Compare different mixture batches separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以序列孔耗量趨勢編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。按相同地層、孔段長度和有效壓力分組比較耗量，核對材料濃度與停止條件；用獨立壓水或驗證孔檢查低耗量區仍否存在未被相交的連通裂隙。分開比較不同材料批次的結果。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for successive-hole take trends, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Group takes by geology, stage length and effective pressure, checking mix concentration and stopping conditions. Use independent water tests or verification holes to determine whether low-take regions retain connected fractures not intersected by treatment. Compare different mixture batches separately.","failure":"注意干擾：先前孔堵住入口會使後續孔吸漿少，卻可能留下更遠通道；濃漿用量的重量與稀漿體積也不可直接比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Earlier entrance blockage lowers later take while leaving distant paths, and dense-grout mass cannot directly compare with dilute-grout volume. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按相同地層、孔段長度和有效壓力分組比較耗量，核對材料濃度與停止條件；用獨立壓水或驗證孔檢查低耗量區仍否存在未被相交的連通裂隙。分開比較不同材料批次的結果。","textEn":"Group takes by geology, stage length and effective pressure, checking mix concentration and stopping conditions. Use independent water tests or verification holes to determine whether low-take regions retain connected fractures not intersected by treatment. Compare different mixture batches separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以序列孔耗量趨勢編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。按相同地層、孔段長度和有效壓力分組比較耗量，核對材料濃度與停止條件；用獨立壓水或驗證孔檢查低耗量區仍否存在未被相交的連通裂隙。分開比較不同材料批次的結果。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for successive-hole take trends, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Group takes by geology, stage length and effective pressure, checking mix concentration and stopping conditions. Use independent water tests or verification holes to determine whether low-take regions retain connected fractures not intersected by treatment. Compare different mixture batches separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「序列孔耗量趨勢」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Successive-hole take trends\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。","按相同地層、孔段長度和有效壓力分組比較耗量，核對材料濃度與停止條件；用獨立壓水或驗證孔檢查低耗量區仍否存在未被相交的連通裂隙。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures.","Group takes by geology, stage length and effective pressure, checking mix concentration and stopping conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按相同地層、孔段長度和有效壓力分組比較耗量，核對材料濃度與停止條件；用獨立壓水或驗證孔檢查低耗量區仍否存在未被相交的連通裂隙。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Group takes by geology, stage length and effective pressure, checking mix concentration and stopping conditions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b237-v15-36","title":"序列孔耗量趨勢：失效診斷","titleEn":"Successive-hole take trends: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「序列孔耗量趨勢」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Successive-hole take trends” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"先前孔堵住入口會使後續孔吸漿少，卻可能留下更遠通道；濃漿用量的重量與稀漿體積也不可直接比較。只追求下降曲線會導致錯誤完工判讀。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Earlier entrance blockage lowers later take while leaving distant paths, and dense-grout mass cannot directly compare with dilute-grout volume. Pursuing a falling curve alone can therefore lead to an incorrect completion assessment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只追求下降曲線會導致錯誤完工判讀。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pursuing a falling curve alone can therefore lead to an incorrect completion assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"先前孔堵住入口會使後續孔吸漿少，卻可能留下更遠通道；濃漿用量的重量與稀漿體積也不可直接比較。只追求下降曲線會導致錯誤完工判讀。","textEn":"Earlier entrance blockage lowers later take while leaving distant paths, and dense-grout mass cannot directly compare with dilute-grout volume. Pursuing a falling curve alone can therefore lead to an incorrect completion assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「序列孔耗量趨勢」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Successive-hole take trends\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先前孔堵住入口會使後續孔吸漿少，卻可能留下更遠通道；濃漿用量的重量與稀漿體積也不可直接比較。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。"],"optionsEn":["Earlier entrance blockage lowers later take while leaving distant paths, and dense-grout mass cannot directly compare with dilute-grout volume.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先前孔堵住入口會使後續孔吸漿少，卻可能留下更遠通道；濃漿用量的重量與稀漿體積也不可直接比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Earlier entrance blockage lowers later take while leaving distant paths, and dense-grout mass cannot directly compare with dilute-grout volume. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b237-v15-37","title":"獨立驗證與統計分布：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Independent verification and distributions: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「獨立驗證與統計分布」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Independent verification and distributions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"帷幕驗證應以水力性能與空間覆蓋為主，不能只重用施工過程數據。裂隙岩體常有偏態分布，平均值會被少數高透水段支配，需保留位置。 假設五孔段在近似線性流況下，按1 MPa有效試壓標準化的單位孔長流量為1、1、2、3、20 L/(min·m)。平均(1+1+2+3+20)/5=5.4 L/(min·m)，中位2 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數，異常高值不能因中位低而刪除。 低中位值可能掩蓋穿越整個帷幕的單一高透水帶，而高值也可能是測試漏流。缺乏位置與原始曲線時，統計不能分辨真正缺口和儀器假象。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「獨立驗證與統計分布」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Curtain verification prioritizes hydraulic performance and coverage rather than reusing process records. Fractured rock commonly has skewed results, so a few conductive stages dominate means and locations must remain visible. Assume five stage flows per unit length, linearly normalized to effective test pressure 1 MPa under approximately linear flow, are 1, 1, 2, 3 and 20 L/(min·m). Mean (1+1+2+3+20)/5 is 5.4 L/(min·m) and median is 2 L/(min·m). These are not direct permeability coefficients; the high value cannot be discarded because the median is low. A low median can hide one permeable band crossing the curtain, while a high value can reflect test leakage. Without location and raw curves, statistics cannot distinguish a real gap from an instrumentation artifact. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Independent verification and distributions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設五孔段在近似線性流況下，按1 MPa有效試壓標準化的單位孔長流量為1、1、2、3、20 L/(min·m)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume five stage flows per unit length, linearly normalized to effective test pressure 1 MPa under approximately linear flow, are 1, 1, 2, 3 and 20 L/(min·m).","failure":"常見誤解：「驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「獨立驗證與統計分布」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Independent verification and distributions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-37-k1","title":"獨立驗證與統計分布","titleEn":"Independent verification and distributions","text":"帷幕驗證應以水力性能與空間覆蓋為主，不能只重用施工過程數據。裂隙岩體常有偏態分布，平均值會被少數高透水段支配，需保留位置。","textEn":"Curtain verification prioritizes hydraulic performance and coverage rather than reusing process records. Fractured rock commonly has skewed results, so a few conductive stages dominate means and locations must remain visible.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「獨立驗證與統計分布」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Independent verification and distributions\" is correct?","options":["驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。","帷幕驗證應以水力性能與空間覆蓋為主，不能只重用施工過程數據。","水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。"],"optionsEn":["A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored.","Curtain verification prioritizes hydraulic performance and coverage rather than reusing process records.","Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"帷幕驗證應以水力性能與空間覆蓋為主，不能只重用施工過程數據。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Curtain verification prioritizes hydraulic performance and coverage rather than reusing process records. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b237-v15-38","title":"獨立驗證與統計分布：定量估算","titleEn":"Independent verification and distributions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「獨立驗證與統計分布」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Independent verification and distributions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設五孔段在近似線性流況下，按1 MPa有效試壓標準化的單位孔長流量為1、1、2、3、20 L/(min·m)。平均(1+1+2+3+20)/5=5.4 L/(min·m)，中位2 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數，異常高值不能因中位低而刪除。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume five stage flows per unit length, linearly normalized to effective test pressure 1 MPa under approximately linear flow, are 1, 1, 2, 3 and 20 L/(min·m). Mean (1+1+2+3+20)/5 is 5.4 L/(min·m) and median is 2 L/(min·m). These are not direct permeability coefficients; the high value cannot be discarded because the median is low. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將驗證孔獨立於施工孔選址，繪出每孔段結果與不確定度；同時報平均、中位和高值位置，對高值回查地質連通及測試完整性，避免只用摘要統計宣布合格。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Locate verification holes independently from treatment holes and map stage results with uncertainty.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設五孔段在近似線性流況下，按1 MPa有效試壓標準化的單位孔長流量為1、1、2、3、20 L/(min·m)。平均(1+1+2+3+20)/5=5.4 L/(min·m)，中位2 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數，異常高值不能因中位低而刪除。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume five stage flows per unit length, linearly normalized to effective test pressure 1 MPa under approximately linear flow, are 1, 1, 2, 3 and 20 L/(min·m). Mean (1+1+2+3+20)/5 is 5.4 L/(min·m) and median is 2 L/(min·m). These are not direct permeability coefficients; the high value cannot be discarded because the median is low.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「獨立驗證與統計分布」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Independent verification and distributions\", which statement holds?","options":["漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。","吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設五孔段在近似線性流況下，按1 MPa有效試壓標準化的單位孔長流量為1、1、2、3、20 L/(min·m)。"],"optionsEn":["Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient.","A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume five stage flows per unit length, linearly normalized to effective test pressure 1 MPa under approximately linear flow, are 1, 1, 2, 3 and 20 L/(min·m)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設五孔段在近似線性流況下，按1 MPa有效試壓標準化的單位孔長流量為1、1、2、3、20 L/(min·m)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume five stage flows per unit length, linearly normalized to effective test pressure 1 MPa under approximately linear flow, are 1, 1, 2, 3 and 20 L/(min·m). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b237-v15-39","title":"獨立驗證與統計分布：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Independent verification and distributions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「獨立驗證與統計分布」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Independent verification and distributions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將驗證孔獨立於施工孔選址，繪出每孔段結果與不確定度；同時報平均、中位和高值位置，對高值回查地質連通及測試完整性，避免只用摘要統計宣布合格。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Locate verification holes independently from treatment holes and map stage results with uncertainty. Report mean, median and high-value locations, investigating geology and test integrity at extremes instead of declaring success from summary statistics alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以獨立驗證與統計分布編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將驗證孔獨立於施工孔選址，繪出每孔段結果與不確定度；同時報平均、中位和高值位置，對高值回查地質連通及測試完整性，避免只用摘要統計宣布合格。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for independent verification and distributions, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Locate verification holes independently from treatment holes and map stage results with uncertainty. Report mean, median and high-value locations, investigating geology and test integrity at extremes instead of declaring success from summary statistics alone.","failure":"注意干擾：低中位值可能掩蓋穿越整個帷幕的單一高透水帶，而高值也可能是測試漏流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A low median can hide one permeable band crossing the curtain, while a high value can reflect test leakage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將驗證孔獨立於施工孔選址，繪出每孔段結果與不確定度；同時報平均、中位和高值位置，對高值回查地質連通及測試完整性，避免只用摘要統計宣布合格。","textEn":"Locate verification holes independently from treatment holes and map stage results with uncertainty. Report mean, median and high-value locations, investigating geology and test integrity at extremes instead of declaring success from summary statistics alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以獨立驗證與統計分布編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將驗證孔獨立於施工孔選址，繪出每孔段結果與不確定度；同時報平均、中位和高值位置，對高值回查地質連通及測試完整性，避免只用摘要統計宣布合格。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for independent verification and distributions, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Locate verification holes independently from treatment holes and map stage results with uncertainty. Report mean, median and high-value locations, investigating geology and test integrity at extremes instead of declaring success from summary statistics alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「獨立驗證與統計分布」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Independent verification and distributions\"?","options":["將驗證孔獨立於施工孔選址，繪出每孔段結果與不確定度；同時報平均、中位和高值位置，對高值回查地質連通及測試完整性，避免只用摘要統計宣布合格。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。"],"optionsEn":["Locate verification holes independently from treatment holes and map stage results with uncertainty.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將驗證孔獨立於施工孔選址，繪出每孔段結果與不確定度；同時報平均、中位和高值位置，對高值回查地質連通及測試完整性，避免只用摘要統計宣布合格。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Locate verification holes independently from treatment holes and map stage results with uncertainty. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b237-v15-40","title":"獨立驗證與統計分布：失效診斷","titleEn":"Independent verification and distributions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"prerequisiteIds":["b237-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「獨立驗證與統計分布」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Independent verification and distributions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"低中位值可能掩蓋穿越整個帷幕的單一高透水帶，而高值也可能是測試漏流。缺乏位置與原始曲線時，統計不能分辨真正缺口和儀器假象。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A low median can hide one permeable band crossing the curtain, while a high value can reflect test leakage. Without location and raw curves, statistics cannot distinguish a real gap from an instrumentation artifact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：缺乏位置與原始曲線時，統計不能分辨真正缺口和儀器假象。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Without location and raw curves, statistics cannot distinguish a real gap from an instrumentation artifact.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b237-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"低中位值可能掩蓋穿越整個帷幕的單一高透水帶，而高值也可能是測試漏流。缺乏位置與原始曲線時，統計不能分辨真正缺口和儀器假象。","textEn":"A low median can hide one permeable band crossing the curtain, while a high value can reflect test leakage. Without location and raw curves, statistics cannot distinguish a real gap from an instrumentation artifact.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]},{"id":"b237-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「獨立驗證與統計分布」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Independent verification and distributions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","低中位值可能掩蓋穿越整個帷幕的單一高透水帶，而高值也可能是測試漏流。","水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A low median can hide one permeable band crossing the curtain, while a high value can reflect test leakage.","Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低中位值可能掩蓋穿越整個帷幕的單一高透水帶，而高值也可能是測試漏流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A low median can hide one permeable band crossing the curtain, while a high value can reflect test leakage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-grout","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals","v15s-usace-gravity"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
